{
  "store": {
    "shape:SdkuWQNIXi_d0o8aqyAf4": {
      "x": 37.05019031872757,
      "y": 42.94096272159703,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:SdkuWQNIXi_d0o8aqyAf4",
      "type": "atom",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "stance",
        "text": "I keep hearing the same metaphor, offered as though it were simply how things are: attention is a resource, spent like currency, and the discipline of a life is mostly a discipline of budgeting it.",
        "sourceId": "001-received-view",
        "created": "2026-07-30",
        "ordinal": 1
      },
      "parentId": "shape:NrfEUK3ihwKQcQ7AYYYqI",
      "index": "a1",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:6ywKw1_wwV1slSL97C46G": {
      "x": 760,
      "y": 48,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:6ywKw1_wwV1slSL97C46G",
      "type": "atom",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "untyped",
        "text": "The attention economy names something real: that noticing costs, that a mind spread thin produces thin noticing, and that no one attends to everything at once. This much I want to hold onto, even as I argue against the metaphor built on top of it.",
        "sourceId": "003-ground-the-economy",
        "created": "2026-07-30",
        "ordinal": 3
      },
      "parentId": "shape:NrfEUK3ihwKQcQ7AYYYqI",
      "index": "a3Ugw",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:xvsQDoxDWtBU84iENlxRn": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:xvsQDoxDWtBU84iENlxRn",
      "type": "frame",
      "props": {
        "w": 784,
        "h": 1040,
        "name": "Received",
        "color": "black"
      },
      "parentId": "page:rzZiePRRfcB3TrrCNiMbE",
      "index": "a1QzD",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:-pbRkVShnaPD5EIWrglmj": {
      "x": 760,
      "y": 296,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:-pbRkVShnaPD5EIWrglmj",
      "type": "atom",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "untyped",
        "text": "Under the metabolic view, rest still matters, but so does what gets carried in: the discipline is not withdrawal but composition, the slow work of choosing a diet of claims and figures and long clausal sentences the mind can actually break down, hold, and eventually turn into something of its own—which is, I think, the only definition of understanding I still trust, and the only reason I keep writing sentences this long instead of shorter ones that would spend less and carry less as well.",
        "sourceId": "012-a-diet-a-practice-can-hold",
        "created": "2026-07-30",
        "ordinal": 12
      },
      "parentId": "shape:OrypP3apbvLqca33-xLSd",
      "index": "a6hSX",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:GE9tKRRi9zwqN5e6gCdFe": {
      "x": 405.0501903187276,
      "y": 42.94096272159703,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:GE9tKRRi9zwqN5e6gCdFe",
      "type": "atom",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "claim",
        "text": "Pay attention, we say, as if the paying settled something—as if the mind kept a ledger, and the ledger, once emptied, simply closed for the day.",
        "sourceId": "002-pay-attention",
        "created": "2026-07-30",
        "ordinal": 2
      },
      "parentId": "shape:NrfEUK3ihwKQcQ7AYYYqI",
      "index": "a2lLU",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:uQU_YmtGpyijix8pNOwIn": {
      "x": 24,
      "y": 296,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:uQU_YmtGpyijix8pNOwIn",
      "type": "atom",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "untyped",
        "text": "So I no longer ask how to protect my attention, as though guarding a balance, but what I am asking it to metabolize, and whether the diet I am feeding it—the feeds, the fragments, the endless untethered paragraphs—is a diet a practice can hold, and tend, rather than merely survive.",
        "sourceId": "010-the-stance",
        "created": "2026-07-30",
        "ordinal": 10
      },
      "parentId": "shape:OrypP3apbvLqca33-xLSd",
      "index": "a4BRM",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:KkxJEL8Y9OgJz-5QCuok-": {
      "x": -600,
      "y": 1240,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:KkxJEL8Y9OgJz-5QCuok-",
      "type": "atom",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "untyped",
        "text": "This is the seam I want to work: not spending but metabolizing, not depletion but digestion, and the difference is not decorative—it changes what discipline is for.",
        "sourceId": "006-the-seam",
        "created": "2026-07-31",
        "ordinal": 6
      },
      "parentId": "page:rzZiePRRfcB3TrrCNiMbE",
      "index": "a9c4I",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:mvQChH55bL7zHsD_XufNq": {
      "x": -600,
      "y": 3224,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:mvQChH55bL7zHsD_XufNq",
      "type": "atom",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "move",
        "text": "2026-07-19 — “ruminate” already does this work for me. To ruminate is, literally, to chew again. The vocabulary of digestion is sitting inside the vocabulary of thought, waiting to be noticed and tended.",
        "sourceId": "notes-2",
        "created": "2026-07-31",
        "ordinal": 14
      },
      "parentId": "page:rzZiePRRfcB3TrrCNiMbE",
      "index": "aHJUH",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:5h56M-S2JwBpdmDcUTSaB": {
      "x": 392,
      "y": 296,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:5h56M-S2JwBpdmDcUTSaB",
      "type": "atom",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "untyped",
        "text": "Under the spending view, rest is the only cure, and so we are told to unplug, to detox, to abstain—language borrowed wholesale from addiction, as though the mind were an account to be left alone until it refilled itself.",
        "sourceId": "011-borrowed-from-addiction",
        "created": "2026-07-30",
        "ordinal": 11
      },
      "parentId": "shape:OrypP3apbvLqca33-xLSd",
      "index": "a52tz",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "user:vq8nLR3ErvsQSb6j-dziI": {
      "name": "",
      "color": "#FF802B",
      "imageUrl": "",
      "meta": {},
      "id": "user:vq8nLR3ErvsQSb6j-dziI",
      "typeName": "user"
    },
    "shape:f79kIxp3mfh0cOk4RiolA": {
      "x": 392,
      "y": 48,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:f79kIxp3mfh0cOk4RiolA",
      "type": "atom",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "figure",
        "text": "A wallet has one operation: subtraction. A gut has dozens—it selects, it ferments, it refuses, it stores, it converts one thing into another thing entirely, and none of this shows up as a number going down.",
        "sourceId": "008-what-digestion-does",
        "created": "2026-07-30",
        "ordinal": 8
      },
      "parentId": "shape:OrypP3apbvLqca33-xLSd",
      "index": "a21tv",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "page:rzZiePRRfcB3TrrCNiMbE": {
      "meta": {},
      "id": "page:rzZiePRRfcB3TrrCNiMbE",
      "name": "Delta",
      "index": "a21Hj",
      "typeName": "page"
    },
    "shape:lDYlSxhg2sFloghKWW_pf": {
      "x": -600,
      "y": 1488,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:lDYlSxhg2sFloghKWW_pf",
      "type": "atom",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "figure",
        "text": "Picture the gut, not the wallet—the figure worth carrying is a long, coiled, patient organ that does not care how much arrives at once so much as what it is asked to break down, and how well it was fed in the years before the test.",
        "sourceId": "f-007",
        "created": "2026-07-31",
        "ordinal": 7
      },
      "parentId": "page:rzZiePRRfcB3TrrCNiMbE",
      "index": "aA5Cn",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:XbkHp-rAQvOifaAImYEjj": {
