        "color": "black"
      },
      "parentId": "page:rzZiePRRfcB3TrrCNiMbE",
      "index": "a2lmM",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:nD5Is3m8VMiZ0T5O-Eur7": {
      "x": -600,
      "y": 2728,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:nD5Is3m8VMiZ0T5O-Eur7",
      "type": "atom",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "untyped",
        "text": "Under the metabolic view, rest still matters, but so does what gets carried in: the discipline is not withdrawal but composition, the slow work of choosing a diet of claims and figures and long clausal sentences the mind can actually break down, hold, and eventually turn into something of its own—which is, I think, the only definition of understanding I still trust, and the only reason I keep writing sentences this long instead of shorter ones that would spend less and carry less as well.",
        "sourceId": "012-a-diet-a-practice-can-hold",
        "created": "2026-07-31",
        "ordinal": 12
      },
      "parentId": "page:rzZiePRRfcB3TrrCNiMbE",
      "index": "aF0CU",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:8ZtEk6vACTo9YDDe5rKhQ": {
      "x": 392,
      "y": 272,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:8ZtEk6vACTo9YDDe5rKhQ",
      "type": "atom",
      "parentId": "shape:xvsQDoxDWtBU84iENlxRn",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "stance",
        "text": "A mind spread thin produces thin noticing.",
        "sourceId": "r-004",
        "created": "2026-07-31",
        "ordinal": 4
      },
      "index": "a4zpY",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:Hl_fV3LtQ5rvFSHgOVBzJ": {
      "x": -600,
      "y": 992,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:Hl_fV3LtQ5rvFSHgOVBzJ",
      "type": "atom",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "move",
        "text": "But a resource, once spent, is gone—while attention, oddly, comes back changed rather than emptied, the way a stomach does not vanish after a meal but sets to work on what it was given.",
        "sourceId": "005-the-turn",
        "created": "2026-07-31",
        "ordinal": 5
      },
      "parentId": "page:rzZiePRRfcB3TrrCNiMbE",
      "index": "a8iuj",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:_qgvBQUOyFFQ0YtNJjXEY": {
      "x": -600,
      "y": 496,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:_qgvBQUOyFFQ0YtNJjXEY",
      "type": "atom",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "claim",
        "text": "The attention economy names something real: that noticing costs, that a mind spread thin produces thin noticing, and that no one attends to everything at once. This much I want to hold onto, even as I argue against the metaphor built on top of it.",
        "sourceId": "003-ground-the-economy",
        "created": "2026-07-31",
        "ordinal": 3
      },
      "parentId": "page:rzZiePRRfcB3TrrCNiMbE",
      "index": "a6ExU",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:inWNoPuYFi6GlYyy9o3xD": {
      "x": 368,
      "y": 992,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:inWNoPuYFi6GlYyy9o3xD",
      "type": "atom",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "untyped",
        "text": "2026-07-19 — “ruminate” already does this work for me. To ruminate is, literally, to chew again. The vocabulary of digestion is sitting inside the vocabulary of thought, waiting to be noticed and tended.",
        "sourceId": "notes-2",
        "created": "2026-07-30",
        "ordinal": 14
      },
      "parentId": "page:page",
      "index": "aT0n6",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:OqfaTEDu6cK3GlKzbqFE_": {
      "x": -600,
      "y": 1736,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:OqfaTEDu6cK3GlKzbqFE_",
      "type": "atom",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "untyped",
        "text": "A wallet has one operation: subtraction. A gut has dozens—it selects, it ferments, it refuses, it stores, it converts one thing into another thing entirely, and none of this shows up as a number going down.",
        "sourceId": "008-what-digestion-does",
        "created": "2026-07-31",
        "ordinal": 8
      },
      "parentId": "page:rzZiePRRfcB3TrrCNiMbE",
      "index": "aBbtz",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:Mj-wgi5H69D9UQ97MvI_x": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": 992,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:Mj-wgi5H69D9UQ97MvI_x",
      "type": "atom",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "stance",
        "text": "2026-07-14 — the wallet metaphor is Puritan in disguise: spend wisely, save diligently, guard the balance. It smuggles in a whole ethics of scarcity that the digestive metaphor simply refuses.",
        "sourceId": "notes-1",
        "created": "2026-07-30",
        "ordinal": 13
      },
      "parentId": "page:page",
      "index": "aSIUo",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:Gyu4lpEnHnvSXkD86lRby": {
      "x": 24,
      "y": 48,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:Gyu4lpEnHnvSXkD86lRby",
      "type": "atom",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "move",
        "text": "Picture the gut, not the wallet—the figure worth carrying is a long, coiled, patient organ that does not care how much arrives at once so much as what it is asked to break down, and how well it was fed in the years before the test.",
        "sourceId": "f-007",
        "created": "2026-07-30",
        "ordinal": 7
      },
      "parentId": "shape:OrypP3apbvLqca33-xLSd",
      "index": "a1",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:anj4zTWs5-dAPKORKWQIQ": {
      "x": 24,
      "y": 272,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:anj4zTWs5-dAPKORKWQIQ",
      "type": "atom",
      "parentId": "shape:xvsQDoxDWtBU84iENlxRn",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "stance",
        "text": "Rest is the only cure, so we unplug, detox, abstain.",
        "sourceId": "r-003",
        "created": "2026-07-31",
        "ordinal": 3
      },
