      "type": "frame",
      "props": {
        "w": 1120,
        "h": 540,
        "name": "The seam",
        "color": "black"
      },
      "parentId": "page:page",
      "index": "aWblr",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:j_A4c12Ig36z104f0nyQs": {
      "x": 392,
      "y": 272,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:j_A4c12Ig36z104f0nyQs",
      "type": "gap",
      "parentId": "shape:xvsQDoxDWtBU84iENlxRn",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "label": "A mind spread thin produces thin noticing.",
        "facingId": "shape:8ZtEk6vACTo9YDDe5rKhQ",
        "sourceId": "g-r-004"
      },
      "index": "a7mG6",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:ms0BwMX2NSs_Fsrndw7kY": {
      "x": 24,
      "y": 272,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:ms0BwMX2NSs_Fsrndw7kY",
      "type": "gap",
      "parentId": "shape:xvsQDoxDWtBU84iENlxRn",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "label": "Rest is the only cure, so we unplug, detox, abstain.",
        "facingId": "shape:anj4zTWs5-dAPKORKWQIQ",
        "sourceId": "g-r-003"
      },
      "index": "a6zcUV",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:JBh1P8UH7e8Q3a6tEGfTP": {
      "x": 24,
      "y": 24,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:JBh1P8UH7e8Q3a6tEGfTP",
      "type": "atom",
      "parentId": "shape:0royW5u1PCw0UEktr-ZE7",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "claim",
        "text": "Picture the gut, not the wallet: a patient organ that asks what it is fed.",
        "sourceId": "m-001",
        "created": "2026-07-31",
        "ordinal": 1
      },
      "index": "a1Uk1",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:4ITibj9qBlqUk-nqdzhpL": {
      "x": 13.050190318727573,
      "y": -5.059037278402968,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:4ITibj9qBlqUk-nqdzhpL",
      "type": "arrow",
      "props": {
        "kind": "arc",
        "elbowMidPoint": 0.5,
        "dash": "solid",
        "size": "s",
        "fill": "fill",
        "color": "black",
        "labelColor": "black",
        "bend": 0,
        "start": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 0
        },
        "end": {
          "x": 2,
          "y": 0
        },
        "arrowheadStart": "none",
        "arrowheadEnd": "triangle",
        "richText": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph"
            }
          ]
        },
        "labelPosition": 0.5,
        "font": "draw",
        "scale": 1
      },
      "parentId": "page:page",
      "index": "aX4rU",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:t--CUg-bWWoj55n5IeJ4O": {
      "x": -600,
      "y": 248,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:t--CUg-bWWoj55n5IeJ4O",
      "type": "atom",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "untyped",
        "text": "Pay attention, we say, as if the paying settled something—as if the mind kept a ledger, and the ledger, once emptied, simply closed for the day.",
        "sourceId": "002-pay-attention",
        "created": "2026-07-31",
        "ordinal": 2
      },
      "parentId": "page:rzZiePRRfcB3TrrCNiMbE",
      "index": "a5bMj",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:Yzxn3Ulcksb7hwA-nnZNm": {
      "x": -600,
      "y": 0,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:Yzxn3Ulcksb7hwA-nnZNm",
      "type": "atom",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "untyped",
        "text": "I keep hearing the same metaphor, offered as though it were simply how things are: attention is a resource, spent like currency, and the discipline of a life is mostly a discipline of budgeting it.",
        "sourceId": "001-received-view",
        "created": "2026-07-31",
        "ordinal": 1
      },
      "parentId": "page:rzZiePRRfcB3TrrCNiMbE",
      "index": "a4Qxj",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:eMdG2RB3rOrKHVMjEZY4_": {
      "x": 392,
      "y": 24,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:eMdG2RB3rOrKHVMjEZY4_",
      "type": "atom",
      "parentId": "shape:0royW5u1PCw0UEktr-ZE7",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "claim",
        "text": "Attention is not spent. It is fed.",
        "sourceId": "m-002",
        "created": "2026-07-31",
        "ordinal": 2
      },
      "index": "a2rHv",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:kV5DBjmx7LAzqeZ8ja2N2": {
      "x": 392,
      "y": 24,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:kV5DBjmx7LAzqeZ8ja2N2",
      "type": "atom",
      "parentId": "shape:xvsQDoxDWtBU84iENlxRn",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "stance",
        "text": "The ledger, once emptied, simply closes for the day.",
        "sourceId": "r-002",
        "created": "2026-07-31",
        "ordinal": 2
      },
      "index": "a2QNj",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "page:page": {
      "meta": {},
      "id": "page:page",
      "name": "Page 1",
      "index": "a1",
      "typeName": "page"
    },
    "document:document": {
      "gridSize": 10,
      "name": "",
      "meta": {},
      "id": "document:document",
      "typeName": "document"
    },
    "shape:5QEbM6zOTTCvmWLnCuJe6": {
      "x": 405.0501903187276,
      "y": 290.94096272159703,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:5QEbM6zOTTCvmWLnCuJe6",
      "type": "atom",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "untyped",
        "text": "But a resource, once spent, is gone—while attention, oddly, comes back changed rather than emptied, the way a stomach does not vanish after a meal but sets to work on what it was given.",
        "sourceId": "005-the-turn",
        "created": "2026-07-30",
        "ordinal": 5
      },
      "parentId": "shape:NrfEUK3ihwKQcQ7AYYYqI",
      "index": "a53er",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:aQy5sgnFS_pe5R_FFQfMb": {
      "x": -600,
      "y": 2976,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:aQy5sgnFS_pe5R_FFQfMb",
      "type": "atom",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "move",
        "text": "2026-07-14 — the wallet metaphor is Puritan in disguise: spend wisely, save diligently, guard the balance. It smuggles in a whole ethics of scarcity that the digestive metaphor simply refuses.",
        "sourceId": "notes-1",
        "created": "2026-07-31",
        "ordinal": 13
      },
      "parentId": "page:rzZiePRRfcB3TrrCNiMbE",
      "index": "aG4Lf",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:Sc8Xe6pnwhIecKVfS4g5G": {
      "x": 37.05019031872757,
      "y": 290.94096272159703,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:Sc8Xe6pnwhIecKVfS4g5G",
      "type": "atom",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "untyped",
        "text": "I grant this much of the received view: something is indeed spent when I attend, some capacity narrows under steady use, and the evening mind is not the morning mind.",
        "sourceId": "004-the-concession",
        "created": "2026-07-30",
        "ordinal": 4
      },
      "parentId": "shape:NrfEUK3ihwKQcQ7AYYYqI",
      "index": "a4lNU",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:JG98tOuH9r-ApCdVBp_55": {
      "x": 736,
      "y": 992,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:JG98tOuH9r-ApCdVBp_55",
      "type": "atom",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "untyped",
        "text": "2026-07-26 — open question for the seam: what is the attention-equivalent of malnutrition? Not distraction, which is too flat a word—something closer to a diet of fragments that never gets broken down into anything a practice can hold.",
        "sourceId": "notes-3",
        "created": "2026-07-30",
        "ordinal": 15
      },
      "parentId": "page:page",
      "index": "aU8Hj",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:_4kW7lPiVdDg54v3uP6pF": {
      "x": -600,
      "y": 1984,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:_4kW7lPiVdDg54v3uP6pF",
      "type": "atom",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "untyped",
        "text": "Attention is not spent. It is fed.",
        "sourceId": "009-fed-not-spent",
        "created": "2026-07-31",
        "ordinal": 9
      },
      "parentId": "page:rzZiePRRfcB3TrrCNiMbE",
      "index": "aCPwn",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:heJLX0QaDUS8wDufun9br": {
      "x": -600,
      "y": 2480,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:heJLX0QaDUS8wDufun9br",
      "type": "atom",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "untyped",
        "text": "Under the spending view, rest is the only cure, and so we are told to unplug, to detox, to abstain—language borrowed wholesale from addiction, as though the mind were an account to be left alone until it refilled itself.",
        "sourceId": "011-borrowed-from-addiction",
        "created": "2026-07-31",
        "ordinal": 11
      },
      "parentId": "page:rzZiePRRfcB3TrrCNiMbE",
      "index": "aErn2",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:NrfEUK3ihwKQcQ7AYYYqI": {
      "x": -40,
      "y": -40,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:NrfEUK3ihwKQcQ7AYYYqI",
      "type": "frame",
      "props": {
        "w": 1120,
        "h": 540,
        "name": "Ground",
        "color": "black"
      },
      "parentId": "page:page",
      "index": "aV6Lb",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:UxS7shX-SAXMrfKhDeG3H": {
      "x": -600,
      "y": 2232,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:UxS7shX-SAXMrfKhDeG3H",
      "type": "atom",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "stance",
        "text": "So I no longer ask how to protect my attention, as though guarding a balance, but what I am asking it to metabolize, and whether the diet I am feeding it—the feeds, the fragments, the endless untethered paragraphs—is a diet a practice can hold, and tend, rather than merely survive.",
        "sourceId": "010-the-stance",
        "created": "2026-07-31",
        "ordinal": 10
      },
      "parentId": "page:rzZiePRRfcB3TrrCNiMbE",
      "index": "aDqxU",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
    "shape:szFOcsItC8ZPVBL_XbOJ0": {
      "x": 760,
      "y": 296,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "id": "shape:szFOcsItC8ZPVBL_XbOJ0",
      "type": "atom",
      "props": {
        "w": 320,
        "h": 200,
        "atom": "untyped",
        "text": "This is the seam I want to work: not spending but metabolizing, not depletion but digestion, and the difference is not decorative—it changes what discipline is for.",
        "sourceId": "006-the-seam",
        "created": "2026-07-30",
        "ordinal": 6
      },
      "parentId": "shape:NrfEUK3ihwKQcQ7AYYYqI",
      "index": "a6O6M",
      "typeName": "shape"
    },
